title Caravan appraise -- a loss its author left unmarked is weighed by what came home after it
prompt Keaton set the autonomous loop running: read Kyri and Radiant first, then REMEMBER and the itineraries, close open reds, take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, send each finished increment as its own signed round.
think The reds queue reads clear -- REDS %96 and %97 both closed on the lap before this one, and the ledger's living rows carry no open entry. Standfast is satisfied, so constructive work may open.
think The running thread is unambiguous. The newest log's recommend names the crux exactly: a bearing is a judgment made before the run, and some losses only reveal what they were worth after it, which asks whether a supervisor may ever weigh a loss its author left unmarked.
think The honest answer is yes, and only under a rule the author published. A supervisor that invents a judgment has overruled the person it serves; a supervisor that applies a standard its plan named is obeying an instruction about the arcs an author could not foresee. So the standard lives at the plan, never at the phase, and an author's word about one arc always outranks any rule about their silences.
think The evidence had to be something only the run could produce, or the rung would be the bearing again under another name. The plan's own downstream is exactly that: a lost arc whose followers all came home is an arc the work behind it stood up without. A lost arc with no follower is repaired, since silence about an arc nothing depended on is no evidence at all, and custody-first reads no evidence as repair.
think The lap needed a fifth phase to carry the evidence. client_c peeks the menu in turn 4, waiting behind turn 1, and comes home -- so client_b's lost peek has a follower that speaks for it and client_a's has none. Both losses are unmarked, so the rung below has nothing to say about either and the standard is the only thing that parts them.
think Two guards were split apart during the RED work. Folding the appraisal into the bearing's own spared mask made BearOverrepaired speak for an overreach that belongs one tier out, so the bearing now guards only what its author marked and AppraiseUnweighed guards what this run's own appraisal spared. Each name speaks for its own tier.
obs The measurement is the eighth of the family and the first that weighs judgment. Every count before it names a harm or a disobedience; this names work a run did that its author never spoke to either way, and that the run's own evidence says nobody needed.
obs The settlement keeps three words rather than earning a fourth. The author chose the loss either way -- once by naming the arc, once by naming the rule -- and an operator's action is the same action, so splitting the word would split nothing real. The wire keeps the two apart glyph by glyph, `b` beside `w`.
obs The choir went RED once on `caravan_taper_witness` and never again. Taper ran GREEN standalone immediately after, and the whole 58-rung choir sang GREEN on the very next sing from the same tree. One non-reproducing failure with no root found is a ratchet rather than a booked red, and it is written down here so a second sighting can be booked with two data points rather than one.
obs The council rota doc this lap was item 14, Radiant Style with Twilight beside it. Its playbook is what the round's prose was swept against before the send: leads first, negation, contrast, voice, then the whole read aloud.
loom witness=caravan_appraise_witness phases=5 dependents_repairing=5 dependents_weighing=4 absorbed=2 lost=2 marked=0 weighed_repairing=0 weighed_weighing=1 repaired_spent_repairing=1 repaired_spent_weighing=0 unserved_weighing=1 pairs=16 red_paths_proven=6
loom witness=caravan_suite_witness rungs=58 verdict=GREEN cold_tree=true
loom module=caravan_appraise lines=3155 asserts=216 usize=0
file caravan/appraise.rye the rung -- the standard, the evidence fold, the wire note, and four refusals by name
file tools/caravan_appraise_witness.rish the witness on metal, reading every number off the run and every glyph off the wire
file caravan/README.md the durable entry, so the arc reads whole without the logs
file tools/caravan_suite_witness.rish the choir registration, so no rung of this arc ever sings unheard
recommend keep-going the arc has answered for reach at every moment of a dependent's life, repaired what a fall cost, learned which losses to leave alone, and now weighs the losses nobody spoke to -- so the question standing above it is what a plan owes a loss it can neither foresee nor evidence: a run that weighed a loss spent and was wrong about it has no way yet to say so, which asks whether an appraisal should ever be revisited by the run that comes after.
